linuxmuster-fileserver-verwaltung (7.3.3) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * CI gains the upgrade-smoke job: every push and every release now installs
    the newest published release, writes a realistic share.conf on it, upgrades
    to the freshly built package and fails unless share.conf is byte-identical
    with unchanged mode and still parses through the package's own loader, the
    CLI and the three .example templates on disk are the freshly built ones,
    the package still declares no conffiles, and dpkg --verify, dpkg --audit
    and apt stay silent. The package has no maintainer scripts and no
    conffiles today, so the job is mainly a tripwire for the day one is added.

