linuxmuster-fileserver-verwaltung (7.3.2) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Documentation fixes from the 2026-09-22 test campaign (fresh member
    server, linuxmuster.net 7.3, Ubuntu 24.04). setup, the join and the
    share configuration are unchanged.
  * README 4.2 no longer asks for the deb.linuxmuster.net package source:
    every dependency comes from Ubuntu 24.04 itself, as ANLEITUNG step 6
    already said and every install test confirms. The download example
    names no version any more ("gh release download" without a tag fetches
    the latest release).
  * The installer does not ask for the Kerberos realm on a correctly
    configured server (krb5-config derives it from the DNS domain); README
    and ANLEITUNG say so instead of telling the admin to leave a prompt
    empty that does not appear.
  * Document -P/--password-file for setup, show and repair-acls (scripts,
    cron), and that "show" prints the NT ACL of the share root only with
    -u <admin>: on a member server only smbcacls through smbd reads the
    stored ACL truthfully, and that needs a domain account.
  * show: the hint printed without -u also names the scriptable form
    (-u <admin> -P <file>); -p/-P without -u are rejected with a message
    instead of being silently ignored.
  * Domain accounts resolve on this server only as DOMAIN\name (no "winbind
    use default domain"); README 2.1, ANLEITUNG 8/9.3/9.4 and both
    troubleshooting tables state the exact spelling.
  * ANLEITUNG 9.4: tightening a folder that already contains files needs
    "replace all child object permission entries" - without it a file
    created earlier stays readable for the removed group. README 6 gains
    the equivalent smbcacls commands for servers managed without a Windows
    client: a per-object loop, because "smbcacls --propagate-inheritance
    --delete" leaves the unflagged entries below the start ACL in place
    (verified in the lab).
  * ANLEITUNG step 4 and README 5 check the group with "samba-tool group
    listmembers": "sophomorix-group --info" shows "Members: 0" although the
    members are set (display quirk).
  * Troubleshooting: the level-1 winbind messages NT_STATUS_INVALID_SID and
    "Unable to open tdb .../secrets.ldb" are harmless noise on a member
    server.
  * ANLEITUNG "Server wieder abbauen": net ads leave works with any Domain
    Admins account, and the DNS record can be deleted from the fileserver
    itself by naming the DC instead of localhost; status then exits 1.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0200

linuxmuster-fileserver-verwaltung (7.3.1) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Apply the faircomp package conventions (linuxmusterDEV
    docs/paket-konventionen.md); no functional changes.
  * Build with "make deb" as the uniform entry point (dpkg-buildpackage
    -us -uc -tc); CI builds in the lmndev-runner container that also builds
    the official linuxmuster.net packages, chosen by the changelog
    distribution.
  * Add ci.yml: on every push and pull request compile and lint the CLI,
    build the package in the container and run the install smoke test on
    Ubuntu 24.04 (previously only on tags).
  * Align release.yml with the shared template: the tag must equal the
    changelog version, build in the container, install smoke, GitHub
    release with .deb and .changes, prerelease for -rc tags.
  * Add CLAUDE.md with the working rules of this repository.
  * Commit messages are English conventional commits (type(scope): subject)
    from this version on; the history stays as it is.
  * Settle the licensing note: configuration examples and debian/rules rewritten as
    original work, LICENSE (GPL-3.0-or-later) added, debian/copyright without the
    UNRESOLVED stanza; the repository is public, docs no longer call it private.

